        "baud_rate": 38400,
        "comments": "-> [[docs:techref:hardware:port.serial]] general information about the serial port, serial port cable, etc.\n\nTwo CPUs means two serial ports :)\n  - Ports\n    * JP1: \"WLAN-CPU\" 9109\n    * JP2: \"MAIN-CPU\" 9202\n  - Pins:\n    * VDD (the [] marked pin)\n    * RX\n    * TX\n    * GND (the pin with less solder in it)\n\nOnly RX TX and Ground are needed to use the terminal set up with 38400 baud, 8 data bits, no parity and one stop bit (38400 8N1). Uses 3.3V TTL.\n\nHow to connect to the Serial Port of this specific device:\\\\\n\n{{:media:cisco:wrvs4400nv2_pcb_serial.jpg?200|**PCB with markings for serial port**}}\n\n^ Serial connection parameters\\\\ for Cisco WRVS4400N | 38400, 8N1 |\n",
